      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'A Mackarel Cat is a type of Tabby Pattern with thin darker line variations,
    causing it to look like the fish. However this doesn not make the cat a fish.


    A
    Cat''s genetics is primarily based on the mother''s pattern. Their color is also
    based on the X Chromosome, carrying orange, black or another color besides their
    base color which makes most tri-colored cats female. A male cat will only have
    one X Chromosome, hence only one other color besides their base color. A mother
    cat with mackarel pattern is likely to have kittens with a mackarel pattern. '
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
