  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Email Phishing (Low Severity) - These revolve around impersonating legitimate
    organizations in order to get recipients to reveal sensitive information or install
    malware.



    Smishing (Low Severity) - These revolve around using messaging
    apps to send malicious links. These are often portrayed to come from trusted
    sources.



    HTTPS Phishing (Low/High Severity) - These revolve around the
    use of seemingly secure websites, leveraging the false sense of security that
    HTTPS provides in order to gain access to important information like credentials
    or trick users into unintentionally installing malware.



    URL Shortening
    (High Severity) - These revolve around shortening of links in order to obscure
    their true destination. Said true destinations are usually malicious websites.



    Social
    Media Phishing (Low Severity) - These revolve around the usage of social media
    in order to distribute malicious content on a wide scale or even impersonate
    people, especially trusted contacts.



    Evil Twin WiFi (High Severity) -
    These are WiFi networks that mimic the names of public WiFi networks. If a device
    connects to this network it will open a backdoor for hackers into the device.



    Fake
    Files (High Severity) - These are executable files or .exe files that are disguised
    as another file type .png, .docx, .pdf etc. This tricks the victim into downloading
    malware into their device.



'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
