      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Contrary to popular belief, crabs aren\u2019t naturally aggressive creatures
    most of their so-called crab mentallity, that is referenced in the Home Economics
    books of Filipino children, comes from how they react to cramped spaces or sudden
    threats. In the wild, crabs prefer to avoid conflict, relying on quick retreats,
    sideways dashes, and camouflage to stay out of trouble.\n\n\n\n\n\nStill, their
    curious personalities and unpredictable movements have inspired countless metaphors\u2026
    even if they\u2019re a bit unfair to the crabs themselves."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
