      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Fishing or Phishing?


    When first told about the Research Study on
    phishing many contestants thought the study thought it was a study on the topic
    of fish. Despite the rules of the Research Competition, of not having any topics
    that focused on Nature and Environment.


    Phishing is a very serious issue
    in cybersecurity as it focuses on social engineering and the vulnerabilities
    of human behavior, instead of exploiting bugs or or oversights on code.


    Phishing
    is trickery. To avoid it, you must not be fooled. Be weary of the links you click,
    the files you download and the strangers, or even, friends you respond to online.


    Anyone
    can be a victim of phishing, young to old, inexperienced to tech savvy, EVERYONE
    can be a victim. We are all human.'
