  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "A new wave of fake account recovery emails has already targeted and scammed
    more than 50,000 users worldwide. These messages claim that your account has
    been compromised or locked, prompting you to click a link to \u201Crestore access.\u201D
    Once clicked, victims are redirected to convincing but fraudulent login pages
    designed to steal their credentials.\n\nThe scam is highly effective because
    it imitates official communications from popular platforms, complete with copied
    logos, formatting, and sender names. Many victims reported that the emails appeared
    at moments when they were expecting legitimate notifications, making the scam
    even more believable.\n\nCybersecurity experts advise users to avoid clicking
    recovery links sent through email unless they personally initiated the process.
    Instead, users should access their accounts directly through official apps or
    websites. As attackers continue refining their methods, awareness remains the
    strongest defense against these large-scale scams."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
